  "summary_en": "European Commission Communication setting a 2025-2030 judicial training strategy supporting DigitalJustice@2030. It sets 15 actions to build IT and AI literacy of justice professionals, train them on digital-economy law and fundamental rights, and coordinate EU and national funding. No robotics or physical AI content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Action 1: make IT and AI literacy training available to all justice professionals.",
   "Technology should support, not replace, human judgment; training should address AI and judicial independence.",
   "Member States must meet AI literacy obligations under Article 4 of the AI Act when using AI in justice.",
   "Training on digital-economy law including AI Act, GDPR, Product Liability Directive.",
   "Justice Programme and next MFF funding, plus a Judicial Training Dashboard for monitoring."
